It is raining very heavily now.
Five minutes ago I was still at the flea market.
I run quickly into a small museum by the park.
Luckily, museums are always open on Sundays.
I stand in the entrance and wipe the water from my face.
Then I go to the ticket desk.
"One ticket, please," I say to the man.
"That is eight euros, please," he says.
I pay, and he gives me the ticket and the receipt.
"You have to hand in the backpack at the cloakroom," he says then.
"This backpack here?" I ask.
"Yes, that is a strict rule here," he explains.
I go to the cloakroom and hand in my backpack.
After that, I go into the exhibition rooms.
It is dry and very quiet in here.
This quiet is really nice after the loud rain.
